{
    "m_SGVersion": 0,
    "m_Type": "UnityEditor.ShaderGraph.StickyNoteData",
    "m_ObjectId": "b73782fcf4c24d1ea9c9c28dc1bc3cf3",
    "m_Title": "Texture3D Noise",
    "m_Content": "This method relies on a small uncompressed 3D texture (64x64x64 pixels) that only consumes 1.1Mb of RAM. This same texture is used in multiple places througout the B2U environment so the cost is only for sampling the texture. This method is MUCH cheaper than using procedural noise. However, being a single texture, it repeats. While the bubble advection does reduce the tiling a bit, it is still noticable on large flat meshes like lakes or oceans. If the texture has 3D depth like a river or waterfall then the tiling is much less noticable. Use this method if you are targeting low-mid tier graphics hardware. ",
